RISC OS file locations and files.

No XDG directories: the "home" directory is <Choices$Write>, so settings
and saved games go in <Choices$Write>.OpenTTD. FioFOpenFile doesn't retry
a missing file in lower case: RISC OS filing systems are case-insensitive,
so the retry only costs time.

Tar files get the Data filetype before OpenTTD reads them. UnixLib gives a
new "name/tar" file MimeMap's type for tar, &C46, which SparkFS claims as
an image filing system; its Tar module then handles the file whenever it's
looked at, and with OpenTTD's downloaded content it crashed (a data abort
in the module), taking the game down and corrupting SparkFS's memory.
TarScanner::AddFile, which sees every tar before it's opened (and each new
download straight after it's unpacked), changes &C46 to &FFD.

For OpenTTD 14.1. See docs/PORTING-NOTES.md in riscos-openttd.

